  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IWGIA: Support to Protection and Promotion of the rights of Indigenous Peoples (2021 &#x2013; 2023)

Find more information on the Danida partner here: https://iwgia.org/en/</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Indigenous Peoples - Indigenous peoples&#x2019; rights, including collective rights to land, territories and natural resources are promoted, respected and
protected. Outcome: Indigenous peoples (including indigenous women) exercise their rights, including collective rights to land, territories and natural resources. Output 1: Indigenous peoples contribute to and claim their rights in climate action. Output 2: Indigenous peoples in 5 selected countries claim their right to land, territories and natural resources. Output 3: Indigenous peoples have taken steps to exercise self governance.
Output 4: Indigenous peoples and IWGIA engage with international and regional human rights mechanisms and use their recommendations at national level.</narrative>
  </description>
